      "writtenOn": "2019-03-14T22:22:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "--block-write-size is added by itself in previous CL from relation chain.\n\nThis is not needed with --iteflash_cr50_through_servod\u003dtrue because 256 bytes is the default with --i2c-interface\u003dccd.  Though it wouldn\u0027t be harmful to explicitly set it to default, if you prefer.\n\nLeaving out --block-write-size\u003d256 would make this CL roughly double reflashing times via CR50 (when using new code path).  That would be unacceptable, not something that should be submitted.\n\n(Slow reflash speeds for a given Servo type are better than no reflashing support at all, but I wouldn\u0027t make this change if it significantly slows down something that is already working.)",
